# Feature 11 — Copy Team Resubmit Notification

## Goal
When a designer resubmits a request after making changes, notify 
all Copy Team members so they know it's ready for re-review.

## Problem
Currently createNotification() is called when a designer resubmits 
in generate/page.tsx but it may not be sending to Copy Team members 
correctly. Copy Team has no way of knowing a designer has resubmitted.

## Fix Required
1. When a designer resubmits a request (status changes to 
   'submitted' or 'in_review' after being 'changes_requested'):
   - Query Firestore for all users where role == 'copy_team'
   - Create a notification for each Copy Team member with:
     - message: "'{request title}' has been resubmitted and is 
       ready for review"
     - requestId: the request ID
     - read: false
     - createdAt: timestamp
     - type: 'resubmitted'

2. Make sure the notification links correctly to the request 
   in the Copy Team review view

## Where to Make the Change
- Find where the designer submits/resubmits in the codebase
  (likely generate/page.tsx or dashboard/[id]/page.tsx)
- Add the Copy Team notification logic there

## After Changes
- Run npm run build to verify no errors
- Commit and push